Product Speedrun is open. You're free to build, change, share and sell what's here,
including the products themselves, as long as you keep the credit and licence notices.

  Hardware designs        CERN Open Hardware Licence v2, Permissive (CERN-OHL-P-2.0)
  (KiCad projects, CAD models, STEP/STL/OBJ/GLB files, BOMs, everything in
  episodes/*/4-model and episodes/*/5-electronics)

  Writing, images and pages   Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC-BY-4.0)
  (concept art, layout sheets, renders, notes, showcase pages, newsletters,
  everything else in episodes/ and kit/showcase*)

  Software                MIT
  (the show console in dashboard/ and server.mjs, scripts/, tools/, kit/*.js)

The full texts are in LICENSES/.

Copyright 2026 Donald Bell and Product Speedrun contributors. Each episode's ideas
are co-created with that episode's guest, who is credited on its showcase page.
Credit line for reuse: "Based on Product Speedrun episode NNN by Donald Bell and
<guest>, https://donaldbell.github.io/productspeedrun/".

Not covered: the name "Product Speedrun" and its logo. You can sell a product based
on these designs, but please don't present it as an official Product Speedrun product.

A request, not a requirement: if you build or sell something based on these designs,
we'd love a credit and a link back, and we'd love to hear about it.

Some concept art is AI-generated and may not be protected by copyright at all; it is
offered under the same terms as far as any rights exist.
